      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(outbound): backport send poll-default guard",
        "body": "Backports the already-merged OpenClaw main fix for schema-padded poll metadata on plain message sends to the `v2026.6.8` release line.\n\nContext:\n- In `v2026.6.8`, normal `message(action=\"send\")` calls can be rejected as poll creation when the tool payload includes schema/default poll fields such as `pollDurationHours: 1` or `pollOptionIndex: 1`.\n- The runtime throws: `Poll fields require action \"poll\"; use action \"poll\" instead of \"send\".`\n- Main already fixed this in `073343e2e2` / PR #93441 by treating only content-bearing poll fields (`pollQuestion`, `pollOption`) as poll-creation intent for send validation.\n\nValidation run on the backport branch:\n\n```bash\nnpm test -- --run src/poll-params.test.ts src/infra/outbound/message-action-runner.send-validation.test.ts src/infra/outbound/message-action-runner.core-send.test.ts\n```\n\nResult: 3 test files passed, 44 tests passed.\n",
        "branch": "codeclaw/backport-send-poll-defaults-v2026.6.8",
